#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351405 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "306a6506-07dc-5b0c-8392-0268c083fa9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{78}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348878} {:answer/id #uuid "713f1706-9cb1-5ca6-a6d0-c5010467a966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{48}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349489} {:answer/id #uuid "b31a9c8d-a546-5cc5-8480-da64dad9d7dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350034} {:answer/id #uuid "e26e4fa2-211b-5423-80e7-522445eb265c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{106}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350438} {:answer/id #uuid "e818788b-e985-59b3-9afa-d1a2bbb5a35f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{84}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b31a9c8d-a546-5cc5-8480-da64dad9d7dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350034} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f9af1a0-4416-5f2e-9bcd-4b88ecf8616c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "401eab2e-5c7c-5b79-aa17-72b56d139abb" :question/math-academy-id "q-82229" :question/problem "![](images/eb/ebb0b09ffab6ffdff6a04104b09d6904302fdb7580262663b5e0c65bd3f95502.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is enclosed by the the curve $y=(x-1)^{2}$ and the lines $y=x+1$ and $y=3-x,$ as shown in the picture. Evaluate ${∬}_{D}2y\\,dA.$" :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/f2/f26c3e1bbbc268308db8d419bc799ad5349673e97c8828471997a5d36cb94d7d.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x+1}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le 3-x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2y\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2y\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{(x-1)^{2}}^{x+1}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(x-1)^{2}}^{3-x}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}{|}_{(x-1)^{2}}^{x+1}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}{|}_{(x-1)^{2}}^{3-x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[(x+1)^{2}-(x-1)^{4}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}[(3-x)^{2}-(x-1)^{4}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(x-1)^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1}+{[-\\frac{(3-x)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(x-1)^{5}}{5}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =((\\frac{8}{3}-0)-(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{5}))+((-\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5})-(-\\frac{8}{3}-0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{15}+\\frac{32}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
